---
export const title = 'Row details';
export const order = 500;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

import dataSource from '../_data-source.json';
---

<p>
  Set the <code>detailTemplate</code> property to a function of the row to let rows expand. The
  table adds a leading column of expander buttons; an expanded row shows a detail row under it, one
  cell across every column, with whatever the function returns (a Lit template, or a string shown as
  text).
</p>
<p>
  <code>expanded-row-keys</code> holds the keys of the expanded rows (compared as strings, like
  <code>selected-row-keys</code>). The table updates it and fires <code>row-expand</code> with
  <code>{'{ key, expanded }'}</code> when the user toggles a row.
</p>
<p>
  The expander is a button with <code>aria-expanded</code> and, while the row is open,
  <code>aria-controls</code> pointing at the detail row. <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> on it
  toggles the row. Detail rows have an <code>aria-rowindex</code> and count in
  <code>aria-rowcount</code>, but they are not part of the arrow-key grid: <kbd>Up</kbd> and
  <kbd>Down</kbd> go from one data row to the next. Controls inside a detail row are reached with
  <kbd>Tab</kbd>. Rows with details turn <code>virtual</code> off, because detail rows vary in height.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='width: 100%; height: 28rem;'>
    <wc-table id='table-expand' key-field='_id' label='People'></wc-table>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $table = document.getElementById('table-expand');
    $table.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14 },
      { name: 'company', label: 'Company', width: 12, flex: 1 },
    ];
    $table.data = dataSource.slice(0, 8);
    $table.expandedRowKeys = [dataSource[0]._id];
    $table.detailTemplate = row => {
      const detail = document.createElement('div');
      detail.className = 'text-body-medium';
      detail.textContent = `${row.email} · ${row.phone} · ${row.address}`;
      return detail;
    };
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  In a Lit app, return a template:
  <code>{'table.detailTemplate = row => html`<p>${row.address}</p>`'}</code>.
</p>
